.TH "LIBXWIIMOTE" 7 "August 2026" "WiiLand" "WiiLand Manual"
.SH NAME
libxwiimote \- display-server-independent Wii Remote access library

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <xwiimote.h>

.SH DESCRIPTION
The libxwiimote compatibility library manages connected Wii Remotes from
user-space. It discovers hid-wiimote devices through udev and exposes their
kernel input interfaces through the existing
.B xwii_*
API. It does not require, connect to, or route events through Wayland, X.org,
XWayland, or any other display server.
.PP
The
.B wiilandd
daemon uses this library for ingestion and translates events into Linux uinput
virtual evdev devices. Applications may also use the library directly when
they need finer-grained access than a display or kernel input path provides.
The resulting event data is therefore suitable for either Wayland or X.org
sessions and for non-display consumers; this manual makes no new API or ABI
claims.
.PP
This library provides a simple, but still comprehensive, API to access
connected Wii Remotes. The API documentation is still in process. Please read
the tools in wiiland/tools/ or the header in wiiland/lib/xwiimote.h for
information on the API.
.SH PERMISSIONS
The process using libxwiimote needs permission to read the hid-wiimote
.B /dev/input/event*
nodes for read-only interfaces. Opening an interface with
.B XWII_IFACE_WRITABLE
requests read/write access and may additionally require write permission;
the library does not elevate privileges. LED and other sysfs attributes have
their own permissions.
.PP
The packaged
.B res/70-wiiland-uinput.rules
rule tags hid-wiimote event nodes for active-seat access and supplies an
.B input
group,
.B 0660
fallback. The packaged
.B res/70-udev-wiiland.rules
rule grants the input group write access to wiimote LED brightness attributes
for tools that use them. Install the rules through the distribution's normal
udev configuration; active-seat ACL and group policy determine the effective
permissions.

.SH BUGS
The library does not support all Wii Remote peripherals, yet. Please consider
contributing to the project if you need further functionality.

